      "summary": "I’m a Mechanical Engineer with a PhD in Thermofluid Dynamics, where my research focused on increasing the airflow and heat rejection rates of an induced-draught air-cooled condenser under windless and windy conditions. This was achieved through CFD simulation using OpenFOAM.\n\nRecognizing the rapid growth of the tech world and the immense potential of data and artificial intelligence, I transitioned into data engineering to upskill in these areas and broaden my career opportunities. Recently, I’ve developed a deeper interest in how AI can create value and solve real-world challenges across industries.\n\nI’m eager to expand my understanding of finance and business strategy to complement my technical expertise. My long-term goal is to combine these skills to tackle meaningful challenges—potentially by establishing my own company in the future. In the meantime, I’m committed to learning and growing where I can.",
